                        "autoGenerateProperties": {
                            "description": "Configures how property auto-generation inspects input data.\n\n- `true` / `false`: enable/disable auto-generation. When enabled with `true`,\n  only the first row of input data is inspected (fast, default behavior).\n- Object form lets you scan more rows:\n  - `deep: true` walks every row and reconciles types across them.\n  - `sampleSize: N` walks at most N rows (implies deep). Useful for large datasets\n    where row 1 alone may not represent the schema.\n\nWhen more than one row is scanned, empty values (`null`, `undefined`, `''`)\nare ignored during inference so a single blank cell does not poison a column's type.",
